A||N||2||kornholio||removing decklid pins||||1
Z||000000||kornholio||10-16-1999||08:19 PM||||I can't seem to pull out these pins and move them to the next hole.  Is there a certain way to do this?  My pins have a rod that sits beside it preventing me from pulling them out.  Do I have to push these rods toward the front of the car?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rcn491||10-16-1999||09:38 PM||||These pins are held by the tension of the springs. You cannot remove them until you hold the tension by some other means.<BR>I used a nylon tie down strap that comes with two steel S hooks and a ratchet mechanism for tighten it. One hook attaches to the U shaped portion of the spring below the pin. The other end has to attached to something strong and aligned in a straight line with the first hook. As an example I took off the EGR Solenoid valve and attached the hook to where the dog bone attaches on the V6. There is a LOT of tension on these springs, so be careful and get someone to help you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||10-16-1999||10:02 PM||||With the lid up I just grab and pull the spring back to release the pin.||||reg||1
